{"name":"Buckingham Palace","hex":"#6b5140","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Buckingham Palace","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The official London residence of the British monarch.","The British monarch or royal family."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Buckingham_Palace"}],"entries":[{"title":"Buckingham Palace","blocks":[{"text":"Buckingham Palace is the official residence and administrative headquarters of the monarch of the United Kingdom in London, England. Located in the City of Westminster, the palace is often at the centre of state occasions and royal hospitality. It has been a focal point for the British people at times of national rejoicing and mourning."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Buckingham_Palace_London_Morning_2020_01_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Buckingham_Palace_London_Morning_2020_01_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buckingham_Palace"},{"title":"Buckingham","blocks":[{"text":"Buckingham is a market town in north Buckinghamshire, England, close to the borders with Northamptonshire and Oxfordshire. The civil parish of Buckingham had a population of 14,294 at the 2021 census. The town lies approximately 12 miles (19 km) west of Milton Keynes, 19 miles (31 km) south-east of Banbury and 24 miles (39 km) north-east of Oxford."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Buckingham_Town_Hall_%28geograph_1486407%29.jpg/330px-Buckingham_Town_Hall_%28geograph_1486407%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buckingham"},{"title":"Palace","blocks":[{"text":"A palace is a large residence, often serving as a royal residence or the home for a head of state or another high-ranking dignitary, such as a bishop or archbishop. The word is derived from the Latin word palātium, for Palatine Hill in Rome, which housed the Imperial residences."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Palacio_Real_de_Madrid_Julio_2016_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Palacio_Real_de_Madrid_Julio_2016_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palace"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Buckingham_Palace_aerial_view_2016.jpg/500px-Buckingham_Palace_aerial_view_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Buckingham_Palace_aerial_view_2016.jpg/1280px-Buckingham_Palace_aerial_view_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Buckingham_Palace_aerial_view_2016.jpg/500px-Buckingham_Palace_aerial_view_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial view of the palace during Elizabeth II's 90th birthday celebrations in 2016","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABuckingham_Palace_aerial_view_2016.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Buckingham_House_1710.jpeg/500px-Buckingham_House_1710.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Buckingham_House_1710.jpeg/500px-Buckingham_House_1710.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Engraving of Buckingham House, c. 1725[8]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABuckingham_House_1710.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Buckingham_House%2C_East_Front%2C_by_William_Westall%2C_1819_-_royal_coll_922137_257059_ORI_0.jpg/500px-Buckingham_House%2C_East_Front%2C_by_William_Westall%2C_1819_-_royal_coll_922137_257059_ORI_0.jpg?utm_source=en